# An unpacked extension added in Settings (Cra copies it into Extensions/) and loaded from its own
# folder with chrome://extensions' "Load unpacked" is one extension after every restart, not two:
# the copy stops loading where the folder loads in place (GitHub #299).
# promise: #299
from://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/UnpackedExtension
from://open?url=chrome://extensions/
wait 3
from://debug?pageJS=chrome.developerPrivate.updateProfileConfiguration({inDeveloperMode:true})
from://debug?bcdp=Extensions.loadUnpacked&params={"path":"${FIXTURES}/UnpackedExtension"}
wait 3
# Loaded over the protocol, Chromium drops it at the next start; a reload installs it as "Load unpacked" does.
from://debug?pageJS=chrome.developerPrivate.getExtensionsInfo().then(l=>l.forEach(e=>chrome.developerPrivate.reload(e.id,{failQuietly:true})))
wait 3
relaunch
wait 3
expect-log extension UnpackedExtension is loaded unpacked from its own folder in Default; its copy stops loading there
from://debug?bcdp=Extensions.getExtensions
expect-log bcdp Extensions.getExtensions → .*Fixtures\\/UnpackedExtension
relaunch
wait 3
from://debug?bcdp=Extensions.getExtensions
wait 1
reject-log bcdp Extensions.getExtensions → .*\},\{
